2 CONT
2 CONT [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shu_Lianghe '''Shu Lianghe'''] (simplified Chinese: 叔 梁 纥; traditional Chinese: 叔 梁 紇) born 619 ''BCE'' ad died 548 ''BCE''. According to the Chinese tradition he was the father of Confucius.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Boxia (伯夏), the father of Confucius and Governor Lu (鲁国 / 鲁國, lǔ guó), in present Shandong (山东 / 山東). He was also one of the greatest warriors of his time and would be the descendant of Yi Yin (伊尹) Premier Cheng 
2 CONC Tang (成湯) founding father of the Shang Dynasty (商朝, 1570 ''BCE'' to 1045 ''BCE'').
2 CONT
2 CONT He is famous for having repelled the invasion of Qi in the outskirts of Qufu 563 ''BCE''. He had a very imposing stature measuring over seven feet. He was also physically very strong and it was said that he could lift loads that w
2 CONC ere thought not to be lifted.
2 CONT
2 CONT Around sixty-five, he married a daughter of the Yan family, Zheng Zai, who was fifteen, he had first married a daughter of the Shi family who bore him nine daughters, and from his second marriage, he had a son Meng Pi (zh) (孟皮). W
2 CONC ith Zheng Zai, he begat Confucius. He died at the respectable age of seventy-one, unfortunately leaving his son prodigy, aged three and Zheng Zai destitute.
