2 CONC  to establish his branch of the lineage as being senior, since his direct descendants became hereditary Wenxuan gong beginning with his son, Yanshi [15932]. Yanshi and his brothers were all granted jinshi equivalencies as was done
2 CONC  in the case of Yanshi's son You [15936]. Yi was granted a position as Qufu county zhubu on the basis of his original petition. In 986, he accompanied Zhao(1) Taizong [9002] on his expedition North and drowned when leading horses 
2 CONC across the Yellow river. CBD, 1, 386. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-collection/46406 RMH]
